  "name": "Question 20",
  "problem": "The following table shows the speed $V(t),$ in miles per hour, at which an airplane flies at certain times since its $2$-hour journey began.\n\n| $t\\,(\\text{hours})$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $V\\,(\\text{miles/hour})$ | $150$ | $250$ | $200$ |\n\nApproximate the total distance traveled by the plane using the trapezoidal rule with $2$ trapezoids of equal height.\n\n*Hint: The distance traveled is given by the area under the speed-time graph.*",
  "worked_solution": "In this context, the area $A$ under the curve $y=V(t)$ over the interval $[0,2]$ represents the total distance traveled by the plane.\n\nThe general formula for the trapezoidal rule states that\n\n$$\nA\u2248\\frac{1}{2}[V(a)+2(V({t}_{1})+V({t}_{2})+\u22ef+V({t}_{n-1}))+V(b)]\u0394t,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of trapezoids and $\u0394t=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ is the step size.\n\nHere, we have the following values:\n\n- The number of trapezoids is $n=2.$\n\n- The corresponding interval is $[0,2],$ so we have $a=0$ and $b=2.$\n\n- The step size is given by\n\n$$\n\u0394t=\\frac{b-a}{n}=\\frac{2-0}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nUsing the above values, the general formula becomes\n\n$$\nA\u2248\\frac{1}{2}[V(0)+2V(1)+V(2)]\\cdot 1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the appropriate numbers from the given table into the above expression gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & \u2248\\frac{1}{2}[150+2(250)+200]\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{850}{2} \\\\  & =425.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total distance traveled by the plane is approximately $425$ miles.",
